{"title":"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>\tConsider the curve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/8/778dffab135924064e9b1105d9c3fa466fa6b459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2}y + y^{3} = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/692545ddeefbdf7f006f3aa196d642d8020ac7a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"26\" height=\"39\" />?\n</p><p>\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/405e58fe9cc4a0aad81ccf1391b79d64472d1333.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{dy}{dx} = -2xy - 3y^{2}  \\quad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{dy}{dx} = - \\dfrac{2x}{3y^{2}}  \\quad \t  \\quad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{dy}{dx} = - \\dfrac{x^{2}}{3y^{2}}  \\quad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{dy}{dx} = \\dfrac{2xy}{x^{2}+3y^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"647\" height=\"44\" />,\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>\tUsing implicit differentiation, we differentiate both sides to obtain\n\t\\begin{align*}\n\t\t\\frac{d}{dx} \\left[ x^{2}y \\right] + \\frac{d}{dx}\\left[ y^{3} \\right] &amp;= \\frac{d}{dx}\\left[ 8 \\right]\\\\\n\t\t\\implies 2xy + x^{2} \\cdot\\frac{dy}{dx} + 3y^{2} \\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} &amp;= 0 \\\\\n\t\t\\implies \\frac{dy}{dx}\\cdot (x^{2} + 3y^{2}) &amp;= -2xy\\\\\n\t\t\\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{dy}{dx} = - \\dfrac{2xy}{x^{2}+3y^{2}}}.\n\t\\end{align*}\n</p><p>\t~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2026 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=